  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n`HypoVault`’s constructor sets\n\n```solidity\ntotalSupply = 1_000_000;\n```\n\nbut never mints those shares to any account. \n\n**Intended logic:** the ERC-20 invariant `totalSupply ==  sum(balanceOf[])` must hold, and all share-minting/redemption formulas rely on that invariant to fairly prorate deposits, withdrawals, and profits. \n**Current logic:** an extra 1 000 000 “ghost” shares live in `totalSupply` with zero corresponding balances. Both key formulas use `totalSupply` as a scaling factor:\n\n```solidity\n// fulfillDeposits()\nsharesReceived = assetsToFulfill * totalSupply / totalAssets;\n\n// fulfillWithdrawals()\nassetsReceived  = sharesToFulfill * totalAssets / totalSupply;\n```\n\nBecause those phantom shares are counted but never backed by assets or balances:\n\n* Deposits over-mint: new entrants receive more shares than their fair pro-rata allocation, diluting incumbents.\n* Withdrawals under-pay: redemptions release fewer assets per share because the denominator is artificially inflated.\n\nOver time this stealthily skims value into the void, permanently disadvantaging honest users.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\nIf an initial “bootstrap” is desired, mint those shares to a real account (e.g., the fee wallet) and deposit matching collateral:\n\n   ```diff\n   - totalSupply = 1_000_000;\n   + _mintVirtual(feeWallet, 1_000_000);\n   + SafeTransferLib.safeTransferFrom(underlyingToken, seeder, address(this), matchingAssets);\n   ```",
  "proof_of_concept": "* **Initial State:** Vault starts with 1 000 000 “ghost” shares in `totalSupply` but no balances.\n* **Seed NAV:** Manager deposits 90 TEST and mock accountant reports NAV = 90 TEST, simulating profit or external funds.\n* **Over-mint on Deposit:**\n\n  * Alice deposits 10 TEST.\n  * Fair allocation would be 111 111 shares, but she actually receives \\~124 999 shares (\\~12.5 % extra).\n* **Under-pay on Withdrawal:**\n\n  * Alice redeems all her shares when vault holds 100 TEST. She holds 100% of the real shares in the vault so she should be entitled to all the profit.\n  * Instead of 100 TEST back, she receives only ~11 TEST (~89% loss).\n* **Outcome:** Phantom supply skews both minting and redemptions, permanently diluting real users. This end-to-end scenario proves both sides of the conversion are corrupted by the phantom 1 000 000 shares.\n\nReplace the empty `test_submissionValidity` test with this and run with `forge test --match-test submissionValidity`:\n```solidity\nfunction test_submissionValidity() external {\n    /*───────────  Configure mock accountant & seed real NAV  ───────────*/\n\n    // Allow the mock to accept our vault and report NAV\n    mockAccountant.setExpectedVault(address(vault));\n\n    // Manager seeds the vault with 90 tokens (simulated profit)\n    vm.prank(Manager);\n    token.transfer(address(vault), 90 ether);\n\n    // Mock now reports NAV = 90 tokens\n    mockAccountant.setNav(90 ether);\n\n    /*────────────  STEP 1: prove the ghost supply exists  ──────────────*/\n\n    assertEq(vault.totalSupply(), BOOTSTRAP_SHARES, \"Ghost supply mismatch\");\n\n    /*────────────  STEP 2: Alice deposit & diluted pricing  ────────────*/\n\n    uint256 depositAmount = 10 ether;            // Alice will deposit 10 TEST\n    uint256 navBefore     = 90 ether;            // What the accountant reports\n\n    // Alice queues her deposit\n    vm.prank(Alice);\n    vault.requestDeposit(uint128(depositAmount));\n\n    // Manager fulfils the whole epoch-0 deposit\n    vm.prank(Manager);\n    vault.fulfillDeposits(depositAmount, \"\");\n\n    // Alice executes her deposit\n    vm.prank(Alice);\n    vault.executeDeposit(Alice, 0);\n\n    /*────────────  Check: she got far TOO MANY shares  ────────────────*/\n\n    uint256 sharesActual = vault.balanceOf(Alice);              // ~ 124 999\n    uint256 fairShares   = (depositAmount * BOOTSTRAP_SHARES)    // 10 × 1 000 000\n                         / navBefore;                            //  ÷ 90  = 111 111\n\n    // Inflation ≈ 11 % → sharesActual > fairShares * 1.05\n    assertGt(\n        sharesActual,\n        (fairShares * 105) / 100,                // > 5 % above fair\n        \"Shares were not grossly over-minted\"\n    );\n\n        /*──────────  STEP 3: Alice exits and gets under-paid  ──────────*/\n\n        // Alice asks to redeem every share she owns\n        vm.prank(Alice);\n        vault.requestWithdrawal(uint128(sharesActual));       // epoch-0 withdrawal\n\n        // Tell the mock accountant what the vault is worth right now (100 TEST)\n        mockAccountant.setNav(token.balanceOf(address(vault)));   // = 100 ether\n\n        // Manager fulfils the whole withdrawal\n        vm.prank(Manager);\n        vault.fulfillWithdrawals(sharesActual, type(uint256).max, \"\");\n\n        // Measure the tokens Alice actually receives\n        uint256 aliceBalBefore = token.balanceOf(Alice);\n        vm.prank(Alice);\n        vault.executeWithdrawal(Alice, 0);                    // epoch-0 execute\n        uint256 assetsReceived = token.balanceOf(Alice) - aliceBalBefore;\n\n        /*  In a healthy vault Alice owned **all** the real shares,\n            so she should have been paid the full NAV of 100 TEST.\n            With the 1 000 000 ghost shares still sitting in the\n            denominator, she gets only ≈11 TEST.                         */\n\n        uint256 fairPayout = 100 ether;\n\n        // Assert she was short-changed by at least 50 %\n        assertLt(\n            assetsReceived,\n            fairPayout / 2,           // < 50 TEST\n            \"Withdrawal was not severely under-paid\"\n        );\n}\n```",
